---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: login" description="The first screen of all: signed in, or told exactly why not without leaking which half of the credentials was wrong.">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: every user, before anything else — the
    first screen and, for anyone who forgets a password, a recurring one.
    <strong>What "done" looks like</strong>: signed in, or told exactly
    why not without leaking which part was wrong. The one screen every ERP
    app has and the one where getting the details wrong locks real users
    out. Composed entirely from
    existing components, zero new CSS: <code>.bo-widget</code> (the card primitive)
    centers the form on the canvas, fields are plain <code>.bo-form-field</code>s
    with the <strong>correct <code>autocomplete</code> tokens</strong>
    (<code>username</code> / <code>current-password</code> — this is what lets
    password managers fill the form), and errors use the same
    <a href={base + '/patterns/validation-summary'}>validation-summary pattern</a> as any
    other form. Try it: submit the empty form.
    <strong>Not for re-authentication mid-task</strong> — when a workspace
    needs a step-up credential check without abandoning the screen the user
    was on (confirming a destructive action, re-entering a password after a
    session timeout), a full-page navigation throws away that context; use a
    <a href={base + '/components/dialog'}>dialog</a> carrying the same two
    fields instead. This page is for the one navigation every session starts
    with, not an interruption inside one.
  </p>

  <section class="demo" style="background: var(--bo-color-bg-canvas); padding: var(--bo-space-8) var(--bo-space-4)">
    <div class="bo-widget" style="inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 24rem; margin-inline: auto">
      <div class="bo-widget__header">
        <span class="bo-widget__title">Sign in to busy-office</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-widget__body">
        <form data-validation-summary novalidate hx-boost="false" class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight">
          <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
            <p><strong>There is a problem</strong></p>
            <ul></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="login-user">Email or username</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="login-user" name="username" autocomplete="username" required />
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="login-pass">Password</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="login-pass" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required />
          </div>
          <label class="bo-choice"><input type="checkbox" class="bo-checkbox" name="remember" /> Keep me signed in</label>
          <div class="bo-form-actions">
            <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Sign in</button>
            <a href="#" class="bo-u-text-muted">Forgot password?</a>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initValidationSummary } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initValidationSummary();
  </script>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The details that matter on a login screen</h2>
    <ul class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong><code>autocomplete="username"</code> / <code>"current-password"</code></strong> —
      the standardized tokens password managers key on. Omitting them (or using
      <code>off</code>) breaks credential autofill, which hurts the users who rely
      on managers for strong unique passwords.</li>
      <li><strong>Server-error recovery uses the same summary box</strong> — on a
      failed sign-in your server re-renders the form with the
      <code>data-validation-summary-box</code> alert visible and a message like
      "The email or password you entered is incorrect." Say which <em>action</em>
      failed, never which field was wrong (that's credential enumeration).</li>
      <li><strong>No premature lockout messaging</strong> — if you rate-limit or
      lock accounts, tell the user how to recover ("try again in 15 minutes" /
      "reset your password"), in the same alert, as text — not a dead end.</li>
      <li><strong>The password field never blocks paste</strong> — paste-blocking
      breaks password managers; nothing here does it and nothing should.</li>
      <li><strong>One column, one card</strong> — <code>.bo-widget</code> with
      <code>max-inline-size</code> centered on the canvas; no new "login layout"
      CSS exists because none is needed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{`<!-- inline-size: 100% matters: .bo-widget is a size container
     (container-type: inline-size), so outside a .bo-widget-grid it needs an
     explicit width — max-inline-size alone collapses it. -->
<div class="bo-widget" style="inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 24rem; margin-inline: auto">
  <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">Sign in</span></div>
  <div class="bo-widget__body">
    <form method="post" action="/session" data-validation-summary class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight">
      <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
        <p>There is a problem</p>
        <ul></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-field">
        <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="user">Email or username</label>
        <input class="bo-input" id="user" name="username" autocomplete="username" required />
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-field">
        <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="pass">Password</label>
        <input class="bo-input" id="pass" name="password" type="password"
            autocomplete="current-password" required />
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-actions">
        <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Sign in</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import { initValidationSummary } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initValidationSummary(); // client-side empty-field summary; server errors
                            // re-render the same alert box with their message
</script>`}</code></pre>
  </section>


  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Brand block</strong> — your mark; the framework ships no logo component, it is your <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Form</strong> — a real <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> posting to your endpoint; native validation first, server validation authoritative.</li>
      <li><strong>Error region</strong> — <code>.bo-alert--danger</code> above the fields, rendered by the SERVER on failure (not JS), so it survives a hard reload.</li>
      <li><strong>Secondary links</strong> — reset password, SSO — a cluster below the submit.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /login</td><td>redirect to the app on success</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /login (bad credentials)</td><td>401 → the same form re-rendered with the alert and the USERNAME preserved; never the password</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /login?next=…</td><td>the form, carrying the post-login destination in a hidden field</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Idle</td><td>submit enabled; autofocus the first empty field only</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Invalid credentials</td><td>one generic message — never "no such user" (account enumeration)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Account locked</td><td>a distinct message with the unlock path; do NOT reuse the invalid-credentials copy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Session expired</td><td>arrive with an info alert explaining why, and the original destination preserved</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Submitting</td><td>button disabled + <code>aria-busy</code>; the form is the only thing on screen, so no skeleton</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>the live demo form carries <code>novalidate</code>, which turns off the browser's own constraint validation — with no <code>initValidationSummary()</code> to call <code>checkValidity()</code> either, Submit fires with empty required fields unvalidated and the summary box never appears; the canonical form in the Markup section below omits <code>novalidate</code>, so a real deployment of it would fall back to native browser validation bubbles instead of losing validation entirely</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 1 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/form'}>Forms</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/button'}>Button</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/alerts'}>Alerts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/components/form", "Forms"],
    ["/patterns/validation-summary", "Validation summary"],
    ["/patterns/error-pages", "Error pages (the same canvas-centered shape, when a destination can't load)"],
    ["/components/dashboard#card", "Card (.bo-widget)"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
